Chapter: HdaTone
  cites Kernel chapter HdaAudio

 The hello-world of sound: a short beep out the HDA controller to the
 speakers. Skipped in the battery -- it makes noise and needs a real
 audio device. Run it by hand to hear the machine speak:

   build/compile.ps1 -Src codex/test/apps/hda-tone.codex -Out t.cdx -Log t.log
   tools/codex-vm.exe -kernel t.cdx -mem 3072

 The beep is one stream buffer long so codex-vm's synchronous drain
 returns at once and the program halts cleanly; a longer tone blocks the
 exit until the host finishes playing it (still audible -- see
 hda-play-tone in Kernel chapter HdaAudio for tones of any length).

Section: Body

  opening : [Console, Audio] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "codex beeps"
    r <- hda-play-tone 660 20
    print-line-uni "done"
  end
